      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Willard Trumbull first homesteaded Elk River in 1897, laying the foundation for the community that follows.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://clearwatercountyadventures.com/elk-river/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The railroad’s arrival from Bovill connected Elk River to the wider region, boosting early growth.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://clearwatercountyadventures.com/elk-river/",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Elk River Historical Museum preserves photos and memorabilia from the town’s days as the Trumbull Homestead hunting resort.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://clearwatercountyadventures.com/elk-river/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "During the lumber era, Elk River built the first all‑electric sawmill, marking a technological leap for the industry.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://clearwatercountyadventures.com/elk-river/",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "A lookout tower in Elk River is listed on the National Historic Lookout Register, honoring its scenic vistas.",
